WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.997
(audience applauds)
- You look beautiful.

00:00:01.997 --> 00:00:02.830
- Thank you very much.

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.920
- Oh my god, I love the hair right now,

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.313
oh my god.
- Thank you so much.

00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:07.660
- Yes, and that's soft.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:08.760
I don't know what the hell it's made of,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.200
but it's soft.
- Magic.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.740
- Magic.
- I'll trade. (laughs)

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.490
- Serious, we--
- We'll trade backstage, yeah

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.323
- We'll trade backstage.

00:00:14.323 --> 00:00:15.970
- Yeah, I like that.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.700
- I just want a day
where I can trade outfits

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.607
with either one of you. (laughs)

00:00:19.607 --> 00:00:21.560
- I'm so excited to be
on a couch with you two.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.419
- Well, thank you.
(audience applauds)

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:23.252
- Thank you so much.

00:00:23.252 --> 00:00:25.988
I'm such a big fan, (laughs) yes.

00:00:25.988 --> 00:00:28.520
- I know, I can't express to you

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.640
how much I am going to rub it in

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.790
to my sister.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:31.840
You're welcome, Lisa.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.284
We were talking about female friendships.

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:36.240
Do you have a lot of female friendships?

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.250
- I do, my best friend is Nicole Byer,

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.190
who's been on the show. but--

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.520
- [Kelly] I love her!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.150
- We have a podcast called "Best Friends,"

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.610
and, thank you,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.653
and yeah, we talk about--

00:00:44.653 --> 00:00:46.800
- From this picture alone.
(Kelly and Sasheer laugh)

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.680
- Clearly we're friends.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.513
We love each other.

00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:49.346
- How did y'all meet?

00:00:49.346 --> 00:00:50.380
- We met through improv.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.340
We were doing improv at the
Upright Citizens Brigade theater

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.173
in New York,

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:59.160
and we were placed on a
mashup group with our teacher.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.490
This woman put together different
women on a team together.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.697
And we kind of saw each
other and were like,

00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:04.980
"She's cool," and--

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.190
- Aw, I love that.
- And then we started asking

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.060
each other to perform,

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.747
and it felt like a first
date where we were like,

00:01:08.747 --> 00:01:09.800
"Can we do this again?"

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.170
And we've just been performing together

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.550
and writing together and working
together for like 13 years.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.140
And I hope we have a--
- Well, finding a partner--

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.501
- Long friendship and
business relationship

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:20.878
as long as we can.

00:01:20.878 --> 00:01:24.450
- And it's a rare relationship

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.270
where she's the first person that I met

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.830
where I could see her all day.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.620
We would go to commercial
auditions together.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.370
We would go to improv classes together.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.200
We would go see a show
together, rehearse together,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.940
and then split up and
then call each other,

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.690
Talk about the day that
we just had. (laughs)

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.870
- [Kelly] I love that!

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:42.150
- We were really obsessed with each other

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.410
- You know, what's so beautiful, though?

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.370
It's awesome to have female relationships,

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.560
but it's also, I think,
powerful to have relationships

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.410
with females in this industry,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.140
because it's a very different thing.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.960
Like, I have friends
that don't do what I do,

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.960
and some conversations are interesting

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.130
cuz I'll never know their perspective

00:01:58.130 --> 00:01:59.530
on their life and they'll
never know mine, you know?

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.700
So that's even cooler

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.267
that you have a female to
lean on in this industry,

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.183
cuz this industry can be hard on females.

00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:07.010
(audience applauds)

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:08.480
- So on your podcast,

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.640
with Nicole, you said hot
dogs are your love language.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.473
Is that true?

00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:13.437
Do you like hot dogs that much?

00:02:13.437 --> 00:02:14.718
- I love hot dogs.

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:16.450
I'm a little embarrassed to talk about it

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.910
but I love them,

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.150
cuz I feel like I've talked to people

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:22.510
who are like, "Oh, what's the
best meal you've ever had?"

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.540
And they're like, "This pasta in Italy,"

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.550
or like, "The seafood by the bay,"

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:29.550
and I'm like, "I had a great
hot dog at Magic Kingdom."

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.196
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:31.196 --> 00:02:33.910
Really do, actually, it's a funny story.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.880
Nicole was dating a guy who worked

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.400
at a hot dog shop near
my house in New York.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.710
- Jackpot for you.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.050
- I mean, he like left
the job years later,

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.580
but and then they met,
you know, happenstance,

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.597
and he was like, "Weird question,

00:02:46.597 --> 00:02:48.804
"does your best friend
Sasheer like hot dogs?"

00:02:48.804 --> 00:02:50.900
And she was like, "Yeah, she loves them."

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.320
And he was like, "Yeah, she
would often come alone."

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.251
And I was like, "He
didn't have to say alone!"

00:02:56.251 --> 00:02:57.662
(audience laughs)
That's, he didn't have to--

00:02:57.662 --> 00:02:59.127
- Why'd you have to--
- Drive it in like that.

00:02:59.127 --> 00:03:01.237
- Just say I went there a bunch.

00:03:01.237 --> 00:03:05.333
Don't I tell other people
I was there alone often.

00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:07.200
- And like, what's wrong with that?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.033
- Exactly.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:08.903
- There's nothing wrong with that.

00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.290
I wanted a hot dog.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.123
I went and got a hot dog.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.040
I go places by myself.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.160
That's what happens when you're single.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.580
- I'm an independent woman.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.785
If I wanna hot dog, I'm
going to get a hot dog.

00:03:15.785 --> 00:03:16.802
(audience applauds)
- It also happens

00:03:16.802 --> 00:03:18.790
when you're a single woman with children

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.137
and you're like, "Someone watch them,

00:03:20.137 --> 00:03:21.010
"I need a minute."

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:21.843
- [Sasheer] Exactly.

00:03:21.843 --> 00:03:23.350
- Yeah, I don't want to
surround myself with people.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.183
There are people at home.

00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:25.437
- Yeah, this is a private me time.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:28.080
Me and my hot dog.
- Yes, I love me time.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.780
- I have husband whose idea of a great,

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.470
it was the middle one,
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.032
his idea of a great vacation was traveling

00:03:36.032 --> 00:03:39.670
around the country to all
the baseball stadiums,

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.110
so I decided my role was to figure out

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.570
which one had the best hot dogs.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.403
- [Sasheer] That's a good job.

00:03:44.403 --> 00:03:45.236
- Kansas City.

00:03:45.236 --> 00:03:46.069
- Ooh!

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:47.700
- Kansas City Royals, their stadium.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.620
Oh my god, best.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.260
- Good to know, I'll have to go there now.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.050
- I love that was
something that y'all did,

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:54.530
just go to stadiums, that's awesome.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.467
Was it awesome? (laughs)

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:58.710
(Lily laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.160
Was it more one of those things,

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.387
like I remember with my ex I'd be like,

00:04:01.387 --> 00:04:03.000
"Yeah, hunting is so cool."

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.776
And then I'd be like,
"I don't like hunting."

00:04:04.776 --> 00:04:06.350
(audience laughs)
Was it one of those things?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.380
- Yeah, but the other
husband did the hunting

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.592
and so I did it with him.

00:04:09.592 --> 00:04:11.116
- [Sasheer] You've tried it all.

00:04:11.116 --> 00:04:12.640
- Yeah, I've tried it all.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.260
- Yeah, well, you don't
know which flavor you like,

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.390
that's what I say.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:18.770
So let's talk about your show.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.020
It's called "Woke" and it's in season two.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.560
So for people that haven't
seen it and saw the clip,

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.500
what's it about?

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.830
- So "Woke" is about Keith Knight.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.770
Keith Knight is a real
cartoonist from the Bay.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.210
And he created this show to kind of talk

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:37.120
about his relationship with
his audience and his Blackness

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.240
and how he infuses his
ideologies into his work.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.157
And so the first season of "Woke" was,

00:04:43.157 --> 00:04:46.690
Lamorne Morris, the main
character, playing Keith Knight

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.930
and kind of him waking up

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.760
and starting to see the
injustices around him,

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.080
and like, how does he want to
talk about this in his work?

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.480
And my character is kind of already woke

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.900
and is kind of guiding
him on this journey.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.630
And the second season, I feel like,

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.830
is really analyzing that word

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.830
and really taking apart the idea

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.730
of what is woke and what isn't

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:10.610
and kind of showing

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.810
that there is no right
or wrong way to do it.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.720
Everyone's just trying their best.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.250
And you can figure it out on your own.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.668
But I like that it makes people think

00:05:17.668 --> 00:05:20.730
about that kind of stuff
while also being very funny.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.680
- Absolutely, I love thought provoking.

